{"action": "next_grill_recommended", "at": "2026-09-18T00:58:55+00:00", "data": {"alternatives": ["Close this track and cut v0.3.0 stable: land PR #6, flip the stale release.yml job name, fix the three real contentDescription misses, and push the tag.", "Grill background refresh: widgets only update when the app opens a repository, so a home-screen widget can age indefinitely without the user ever seeing it refresh."], "reason": "The compact slot now tells the truth, which makes the tall path's fixture rows the most visible remaining dishonesty in a Play-published build.", "recommended": "Convert the tall widget row feed to live data and retire WIDGET_PREVIEW_LABEL entirely, so no surface of RepoGlance renders fixture content.", "recorded_at": "2026-09-18T00:58:55+00:00"}, "event_id": "f78ecbcb-2514-4009-b979-ccb5410d6aed"}
{"action": "next_grill_recommended", "at": "2026-09-18T02:55:16+00:00", "data": {"alternatives": ["Reopen pin-model-010. Its locked choice says pinned repos 'form the widget and background-refresh set', but RepoWidget selects its repository from per-widget RepoWidgetConfigStore rather than pins (0 pin references), and no background-refresh set exists at all. Only StackWidget honours the pin clause.", "Convert the tall row feed to live data and retire WIDGET_PREVIEW_LABEL, the prior recommendation \u2014 still valid, but it makes more fixture surface live without addressing whether live data stays current."], "reason": "Making the compact slot live converted a cosmetic fixture problem into a real staleness problem: fixtures regenerated at render time and were always current, whereas a stored snapshot ages with nothing to refresh it and nothing on screen to disclose its age.", "recommended": "Grill widget freshness: give the compact widget a background refresh path and a visible freshness signal. Evidence: updatePeriodMillis=0 on both widget XMLs, no WorkManager/AlarmManager/JobScheduler anywhere and no such dependency declared, and WidgetRefresh.updateAll reachable only from MainActivity (pin/scenario change) and RepoGlanceViewModel (repo opened in app). A compact widget's counts are therefore frozen at the last in-app visit to that repo, and the locked round-2 ledger composition surfaces neither observedAt age nor the LAST_GOOD basis, so an arbitrarily old count renders as a bare number.", "recorded_at": "2026-09-18T02:55:16+00:00"}, "event_id": "7d6e1b82-899e-45ba-a0c0-d6834892bb04"}
